                    "children": [],
                    "answer": {
                      "short": "$3(-4)=-12$ and $-12\\not\\ge-9$. Although $-4\\le-3$, it does not satisfy the original inequality.",
                      "worked": "$\\begin{align*}3(-4)&=-12\\\\-12&\\not\\ge-9\\end{align*}$\nChantelle’s answer includes $x=-4$, but this value fails the original inequality, so her answer is wrong.",
                      "solutionDiagrams": []
